      "drive-closed-pipe-tests-until-closure": {
        "title": "Test downstream closure while a callable writes, yields, or waits",
        "text": "When testing a callable stage whose downstream reader exits, send bounded chunks one at a time after each acknowledgement until the host reports closure or the test deadline expires. A pipe can accept an initial write while the reader is exiting. After closure, check the stage cancellation and final graph outcome.\n\nAlso test a generator that keeps yielding without writing and a generator blocked in a confirmed-started subprocess or stdin read. Schedule the stdout closure watch independently so it can wake a waiting stage. Cancel an active subprocess request and await its terminal acknowledgement before unwinding. Close borrowed readers through their existing ownership path. On native and WASM, assert aggregate success, cancelled stage outcome, and cleanup separately. Preserve structured completions for configured and topology process requests so the WASM success shortcut cannot discard per-stage outcomes.\n\nTest a consumer that closes stdin and stays alive until the generator cleans up. The Node host can detect reader closure by opening the private FIFO with O_WRONLY | O_NONBLOCK and checking for ENXIO, without writing probe bytes or changing endpoint flags. Keep names only for watched FIFOs. Remove their private directory when the graph joins or launch fails, and check for leftovers after the test.",
        "children": [],
        "sources": [
          "src/go/kame/host/posix/stage_io_test.go",
          "src/go/kame/host/posix/stage_io.go",
          "src/go/kame/host/stage_io.go",
