      "preserve-computed-rule-output-spellings": {
        "title": "Preserve both computed rule output spellings",
        "text": "Use `${EXPR}` for full-expression interpolation in Kame double-quoted strings, path atoms and rule headers, and Kash command words, including `${(dirs REPOS)}`. Use `@{EXPR}` in document templates and foreign-shell recipes. Support `(EXPR)` and `${EXPR}` for computed file outputs on explicit `rule` headers. Keep authored declarations and `Rule` constructors on the same output grammar and verify both entry points through T010-27 on native and WASM.\n\nShare text rendering for `${EXPR}` in Kame strings and composed or quoted Kash words. Scalars render as text, nil renders empty, lists render their items recursively with spaces between items, and other values use ordinary display notation. Kash keeps that rendered text within one word. A standalone unquoted substitution retains its typed value through argv conversion and may splice a list. Template `@{EXPR}` uses its own rendering rules.",
        "children": [],
