      "preserve-kash-setup-label-spelling": {
        "title": "Preserve Kash setup labels and expression symbols",
        "text": "Use `KEY: VALUE` setup labels in raw Kash command stages and `with` headers. Preserve `:name` syntax for standalone expression symbols and setup symbols passed to expression-level `run!` and `capture!`. When changing setup parsing or formatting, exercise both Kash setup contexts, confirm prefix-style setup is rejected before a raw command, and check ordinary argv still retains literal label-like words.\n\nWhen the working directory prevents process startup, name the resolved directory and state why it cannot be used. Check missing and non-directory paths through the real native and WASM launch paths. In a `with` header, use `cwd: $repo` to read the binding. A bare `cwd: repo` supplies a literal word, so any failure should name the resolved literal path.",
        "children": [],
        "sources": [
