      "prove-disk-writing-freshness-workloads": {
        "title": "Prove freshness benchmark execution",
        "text": "For disk-writing freshness benchmarks, verify both exact output bytes and the exact file target-reason execute set or process-started events; target-started alone does not prove execution because fresh targets also emit it. Treat a repeated invocation as a no-op only when events confirm that no work launched. For clean self-builds, account for version_generated.go when defining the scanned source set: a minimized actual Kamefile fixture showed that putting it as an explicit normal prerequisite in a group before computing/scanning the remaining sources avoids INPUT_UNSTABLE from the generated file's appearance and yields zero work on the first repeat on both native and Node/WASM. Merely post-filtering the computed result does not remove the glob's watched membership. Preserve the earlier observed caveat that the unfixed clean self-build can rerun its compiler on the first repeat and become idle only on the next, including baseline; do not infer more than verified fixture behavior or claim full self-build timing. For piped-stdin freshness tests, use a discovered Kamefile with `kame -C DIR TARGET`, not `-f FILE` or `-c TEXT`, because run mode forces every rule.",
        "children": [],
        "sources": [
